  "notes": "Live-band retro-soul/funk producer who also runs a four-on-the-floor side project. The documented core of his method is a tracking decision: \"live rhythm section tracked as an ensemble with period-appropriate technique — dry, tight, hard-hitting backbeat, hi-hat 16ths with accented offbeats, tambourine and handclaps doubling the snare.\" So the snare is `hard` transient under a `short` tail, `hihat.base` is 16th at a high fill density with the widest velocity spread in this batch (accented offbeats are a velocity, not a placement), the perc lanes are `tambourine`, `clave` and `conga` at `downbeat`, and the humanize block is an ensemble one at `quantizeStrength` 0.68. He overlaps his best-known artist by design and the difference authored is what his own entry adds rather than a manufactured one: the Silk City house side, which is why `fourOnFloorInChorus` is true and the kick reaches a density of 5, and the covers-album reinterpretation habit, which is the higher `switchUpProb`. The bass is a co-lead and not an 808: \"no 808 in the soul mode — fingered or slapped electric bass playing a complete syncopated line as a co-lead. The dance project instead uses a filtered pumping house sub\", which is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.28 with a full passing-tone set. Harmony is the entry's: \"major-mode funk keys with dominant-7th/9th vamps and blues-scale melodic borrowing … one- or two-chord vamps with extended dominants rather than progressions\", so `maxChords` is 2, `harmonicRhythm` is vamp-dominant and `seventh` plus `ninth` carry three-quarters of the weight. \"Live horn sections as the primary countermelody\" is `answer_lick` at the top weight, and the arrangement is vamp form with stop-time breaks instead of bridges. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 98 (the midpoint of the first-named 70—125 soul/funk band) are INFERRED.",
